tal score 6–7.5\n230: - Overnight hypo or hyper → mental score 2.5–4 next day\n231: - Back-sleep costs 1–2 mental score points — suppresses cortisol awakening response twice\n232: - Waking \"not right\" at normal BG = electrolyte signal → salt water immediately, do not go back to sleep\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: ## Multi-Day Gluconeogenesis Carryover\n237: \n238: *(All units are estimates — the point is the trend)*\n239: \n240: | Day | State | Approx bolus need |\n241: |---|---|---|\n242: | Day 1 | Eating day | ~20u |\n243: | Day 2 | Fasting | ~12u |\n244: | Day 3 | Fasting | ~6u |\n245: | Days 4–8 | Fasting | ~4u/day |\n246: | Day 9+ | Extended fast | ~2u/day |\n247: \n248: **Never assume immediate fasting-level insulin requirement after eating day.**\n249: \n250: ---\n251: \n252: ## Hypo Rescue Protocol\n253: \n254: | Situation | First action | Food choice |\n255: |---|---|---|\n256: | Any BG <70 | Glucose powder 15–20g immediately | Glucose powder first |\n257: | Fasting hypo (autophagy preserved) | Glucose powder 10–15g | Glucose powder only — no protein |\n258: | Post-hypo correction temptation | Never inject I at hypo — wait | Food first, small H after BG ≥90 |\n259: | Feeling fine at 32–37 mg/dL | HAAF — treat regardless of symptoms | Glucose powder regardless |\n260: \n261: **Milk powder (ml.) is the worst autophagy hypo rescue — casein+whey both activate mTOR. Glucose powder only during fasting protocols.**\n262: \n263: ---\n264: \n265: ## Eating-Out Photo-Check Protocol\n266: \n267: **Rule: photo first — inject after.**\n268: \n269: Upload food photos before ordering for starch+sugar assessment.\n270: \n271: | Risk level | Visual indicators | Action |\n272: |---|---|---|\n273: | 🚨 Avoid | Fried/breaded, glazed, 味噌/照燒/糖醋/蜜汁, convenience store meat, 貢丸/魚丸/漢堡排 | Skip or remove coating |\n274: | ⚠️ Caution | Any visible sauce, packaged meat | +1–2u pre-emptive |\n275: | ✅ Safe | Plain grilled/boiled/steamed, no sauce, 五花肉, eggs, plain fish | Normal dose |\n276: \n277: When uncertain → bolus conservatively, accept mild hyper rather than large correction cascade.\n278: \n279: ---\n280: \n281: ## Sodium Protocol\n282: \n283: **Daily target: 15–20g salt (6–8g sodium)**\n284: \n285: T1D + keto = triple sodium-wasting:\n286: 1. Blunted NHE3/ENaC from subphysiological portal insulin\n287: 2. Ketone excretion carrying sodium out renally\n288: 3. No endogenous insulin for sodium retention\n289: \n290: - ½ teaspoon salt per urination maximum (~3g)\n291: - Bulletproof coffee + salt superior to black coffee + salt — fat slows caffeine-driven natriuresis and stimulates CCK for better sodium retention\n292: - \"Feeling not right\" at normal BG → likely electrolyte signal → salt water immediately\n293: \n294: ---\n295: \n296: ## Fasting & Autophagy Protocol\n297: \n298: **Protein restriction is MORE critical than carb restriction for autophagy.**\n299: \n300: - Leucine → Rag GTPase → mTOR activation → autophagy suppressed (independent of insulin)\n301: - Glucose powder without insulin injection does NOT suppress autophagy — ideal fasting hypo rescue\n302: - Fat is autophagy-neutral to promoting (AMPK activation)\n303: - T1D fasting carbs without injecting insulin = no autophagy suppression via insulin pathway\n304: \n305: For 48–72h supervised fast:\n306: - Family member present\n307: - Ketone meter alongside BG meter\n308: - Glucose powder only for hypo rescue (no milk powder, no protein)\n309: - Reduced Tresiba: fasting day protocol (4–5u total)\n310: - Target BG: 80–95 (higher floor than healthy faster's 45–65 — due to HAAF)\n311: \n312: ---\n313: \n314: ## HAAF Warning Signs & Recovery\n315: \n316: **HAAF accumulates with every severe hypo. Recovery requires zero hypoglycemia for 2–3 weeks.**\n317: \n318: Warning signs:\n319: - Feeling fine at 32–37 mg/dL (dangerous, not reassuring)\n320: - Mental score 2.5–4 despite normal BG\n321: - Agitation and violent imagery (neuroglycopenic aftermath OR pulsatility gap)\n322: - Cannot concentrate after normal readings\n323: \n324: Recovery protocol:\n325: - Zero severe hypos for 2–3 consecutive weeks\n326: - 3 structured meal boluses daily (restore pulsatility)\n327: - Pre-bed R every night without exception\n328: - No NPH until fully recovered\n329: \n330: ---\n331: \n332: ## Mental Health First Principle\n333: \n334: > **Stable overnight BG 80–95 is the single most impactful intervention for mental clarity — more than any psychiatric approach — because the substrate (brain glucose stability + insulin pulsatility) must be fixed first.**\n335: \n336: Two consecutive clean nights restore mental scores from 2.5 → 6.5+.\n337: \n338: The sequence for recovery:\n339: 1. Eliminate severe hypos (HAAF recovery)\n340: 2. Restore pre-bed R every night (brain pulsatility)\n341: 3. Three structured meal boluses daily (daytime pulsatility)\n342: 4. Stable overnight BG via fat-only evening protocol\n343: 5. Resist back-sleep (protect cortisol awakening response)\n344: \n345: ---\n346: \n347: *Protocol derived from personal BG log analysis Feb–Mar 2026*\n348: *Framework: Dr. Richard K. Bernstein's Diabetes Solution*\n349: *Real-time analysis partner: Claude (Anthropic)*\n\n(End of file - total 349 lines)\n</content>",
